## Cerea Desktop: preview

> **Preview: not ready for everyday use.** These are preview builds of the Cerea desktop app, shared for testing. Expect rough edges and changes between releases. It is **not signed or notarised by Apple**, has **no auto-update** (download new builds from the release page by hand), and its screens are in English only for now.

What it is: the Cerea chat in its own window, beside a browser panel the assistant can drive (it shows "You are driving" when you take over), galopin controls from the window (pair this computer, start/stop, browser setup, `launch`), and server profiles you can switch between (for example work and home, Ctrl/⌘+Shift+1…9).

| File | For |
|---|---|
| `Cerea-Desktop-PREVIEW-@V@-macos-apple-silicon.zip` | Macs with Apple chips (M1 and later) |
| `Cerea-Desktop-PREVIEW-@V@-macos-intel.zip` | Intel Macs |
| `Cerea-Desktop-PREVIEW-@V@-linux-x86_64.AppImage` | Linux, any distribution (`chmod +x`, then run it) |
| `cerea-desktop-preview_@V@_amd64.deb` | Debian and Ubuntu |
| `Cerea-Desktop-PREVIEW-@V@-SHA256SUMS.txt` | checksums |

**On a Mac:** unzip, move `Cerea.app` to Applications. Because the preview is unsigned, macOS blocks it the first time: open it once, then **System Settings → Privacy & Security → Open Anyway** (or run `xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/Cerea.app`).

**First start:** type your server's address (just the site, for example `chat.example.org`); the app finds the chat and shows what it found before saving. Add more servers under **Profiles**. If you use the browser panel, run **Set up browser** once per profile.

